Hmm, but actually the acceptance message is "Parameter error, the appId is empty or null." Upstream in FederationInterceptorREST getAppAttempts (YARN-11228 patch):

```java
  @Override
  public AppAttemptsInfo getAppAttempts(HttpServletRequest hsr, String appId) {
    long startTime = clock.getTime();
    try {
      ApplicationId appIdentifier = ApplicationId.fromString(appId);
      SubClusterInfo subClusterInfo = getApplicationHomeSubCluster(appIdentifier);
      DefaultRequestInterceptorREST interceptor = getOrCreateInterceptorForSubCluster(
          subClusterInfo.getSubClusterId(), subClusterInfo.getRMWebServiceAddress());
      AppAttemptsInfo appAttemptsInfo = interceptor.getAppAttempts(hsr, appId);
      long stopTime = clock.getTime();
      routerMetrics.succeededAppAttemptsRetrieved(stopTime - startTime);
      return appAttemptsInfo;
    } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
      routerMetrics.incrAppAttemptsFailedRetrieved();
      RouterServerUtil.logAndThrowException("Unable to getAppAttempts by appId: %s.", e, appId);
    } catch (YarnException e) {
      routerMetrics.incrAppAttemptsFailedRetrieved();
      RouterServerUtil.logAndThrowException("getApplicationHomeSubCluster by appId: %s error.", e, appId);
    } catch (Exception e) {
      routerMetrics.incrAppAttemptsFailedRetrieved();
      RouterServerUtil.logAndThrowException("Unable to getAppAttempts by appId: %s.", e, appId);
    }
    throw new YarnRuntimeException("Unable to getAppAttempts by appId: " + appId);
  }
```

Hmm — but upstream at the time of YARN-11228 (2022), FederationInterceptorREST was the "new style" with `invokeMethod`, ThreadLocal caches, RouterMetrics with succeededAppAttemptsRetrieved etc. This tree's version is the older style (clock, simple). RouterMetrics in this tree — does it have succeededAppAttemptsRetrieved? Probably not. The yaml acceptance signals mention only the behavior: route to home subcluster, validate appId with "Parameter error, the appId is empty or null." message.

Let me check RouterServerUtil.logAndThrowException signatures (from router-pipeline-utils commit by another agent).

